\newlabel{sec:deriv-std-parser}{{5.1.3}{29}{Parser}{subsection.5.1.3}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.4}{\ignorespaces The standard derivative-based parser. The forward pass sets \texttt  {expressions[0]}=$r$ and appends \texttt  {deriv} for each character, so entry $i$ is the residual after $i$ characters; a non-nullable final entry returns \texttt  {None}. The backward pass starts from \texttt  {mk\_eps} of the final entry and applies \texttt  {inject} to entries $n-1$ down to $0$ with the corresponding characters, undoing one derivative step per character and yielding the parse tree for $r$.}}{29}{figure.caption.18}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:deriv-std-drivers-rust}{{5.4}{29}{The standard derivative-based parser. The forward pass sets \texttt {expressions[0]}=$r$ and appends \texttt {deriv} for each character, so entry $i$ is the residual after $i$ characters; a non-nullable final entry returns \texttt {None}. The backward pass starts from \texttt {mk\_eps} of the final entry and applies \texttt {inject} to entries $n-1$ down to $0$ with the corresponding characters, undoing one derivative step per character and yielding the parse tree for $r$}{figure.caption.18}{}}
