\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.5}{\ignorespaces The bit-coded construction on the ambiguous example. The forward pass attaches bits to the residual and simplifies at every step. $\mathit  {mkEpsBC}$ extracts the accumulated bit sequence, and $\mathit  {decode}_r$ reads that sequence against the original $r$ to reconstruct the parse tree.}}{31}{figure.caption.19}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:single-pass}{{5.5}{31}{The bit-coded construction on the ambiguous example. The forward pass attaches bits to the residual and simplifies at every step. $\mathit {mkEpsBC}$ extracts the accumulated bit sequence, and $\mathit {decode}_r$ reads that sequence against the original $r$ to reconstruct the parse tree}{figure.caption.19}{}}
